5D4 GUI menu source cleanup — RC2-V2B
=======================================

Classification: RESEARCH UPDATE
Target: Canon EOS 5D Mark IV firmware 1.3.3
Local source baseline: branch 5d4-133-candidate, commit 77bfce0ff4b08b93e0ae6719a883f14ad2ab8a33

Pre-cleanup src/menu.c SHA-256:
3e96bb91c5c2cb3472962bdafa8b92eadddfcded9cee9037900c8f0e1cb3841c

Accepted RC2-V2B src/menu.c SHA-256:
f5466d01b585f59a1071ca9f724355f82f83d10e3ce2a316b85642a5d311714b

Validation:
- build PASS
- menu.o SHA-256 62a53497d813229c6727f2d7039dc2c6402ffa95d7bd19590365a139b46039c7, byte-identical
- all allocated sections byte-identical
- symbol table identical
- magiclantern.bin same size; four differing bytes confined to build_date timestamp metadata
- no functional binary difference attributable to this cleanup

Scope:
- remove trailing whitespace
- remove disabled duplicate BGMT_PLAY block
- remove obsolete commented guimode.ml.menu tuner
- preserve physical line numbering for __LINE__ stability
- retain GUI-event diagnostics, TESTLV/TESTGM/TESTNS instrumentation, TEST90 and stress/profiling infrastructure

No new hardware run was performed for the cleanup itself. Underlying GUI Lifecycle HC1 remains the previously hardware-validated source state. Generated binaries are not included.

